<title>GERMANY: BA agrees two-year Germany pay deal.</title>
<headline>BA agrees two-year Germany pay deal.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways said it has reached a two-year pay deal with the OeTV transport union for its employees in Germany.</p>
<p>BA will introduce a two-tier wage increase with a 1.9 percent rise back-dated to April 1, 1996 and a 1.95 percent increase from February 1, 1997, until March 31, 1998.</p>
<p>The deal, agreed between the airline and the union on January 29, thus runs for a total of two years, a BA statement issued here said.</p>
<p>BA and the OeTV will also start negotiations on performance-related payments in order to make the current pay structure more flexible, the airline added.</p>
